id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    _BASE_VALUES = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # Handle the initial base cases directly for n less than 4.\n    if n < 4:\n        return _BASE_VALUES[n]\n\n    # Initialize the four variables with the base values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3).\n    # These variables `a, b, c, d` will hold fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1) respectively.\n    a = _BASE_VALUES[0]\n    b = _BASE_VALUES[1]\n    c = _BASE_VALUES[2]\n    d = _BASE_VALUES[3]\n\n    # Iterate from the 4th term up to the n-th term.\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b + c + d\n        # Shift the values: fib4(i-4) becomes fib4(i-3), etc.\n        a = b\n        b = c\n        c = d\n        d = next_fib\n    \n    return d", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/48": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/48", "solution": "def is_palindrome(text: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if given string is a palindrome\n    >>> is_palindrome('')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('aba')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('aaaaa')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('zbcd')\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    return text == text[::-1]", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/51": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/51", "solution": "VOWEL_SET = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u', 'A', 'E', 'I', 'O', 'U'}\ndef remove_vowels(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    remove_vowels is a function that takes string and returns string without 